{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And you shall bring an offering, etc.</b> These are the additional offerings stated in the section of Pinchas. And why are they stated here? To say that the additional offerings do not hold back one another." "<b>And you shall bring an offering to YHWH.</b> In any case — if there are no bulls, bring rams; and if there are no bulls and rams, bring lambs (there)." "<b>Seven days.</b> Everywhere that שִׁבְעַת is said, it is a noun — a week of days, שטי\"נא בְּלַעַ\"ז. And so every expression of שְׁמוֹנַת שֵׁשֶׁת חֲמֵשֶׁת שְׁלוֹשֶׁת." "<b>Work of labor.</b> Even labors that are important to you for work and need — where there is loss of money in their neglect — such as a lost item. Thus I have understood from the Tosefta, for it teaches: 'I might think even the intermediate days of the Festival should be forbidden in work of labor, etc.'"], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {2 "the la'az is Old French semaine (or setaine), 'week'", 3 "תֹ\"כֹ resolved as תוספתא (Tosefta) based on the citation formula and content"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:56.893059815Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}